From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean O'Hollaren <sean.ohollaren@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:03:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] FM-1: pitch, tempo, FM depth, envelope and filter wobble on
 the knobs; the drive is gone

The drive did not sound good on a whole mix and is removed. In its place, knobs on the music's own
FM voices (i_oplmusic.c): KNOB 3 pitch (a semitone a click, an octave each way, sounding notes move
with it), KNOB 4 tempo (half to double speed), ALGORITHM FM depth (every FM voice's modulator up or
down 1.5 dB a step). ENV swaps KNOB 3 and KNOB 4 to a second pair and back: the envelope of the
notes (short: they fall away while held; long: slow attack, long release) and a wobble that swings
the filter's cutoff about where KNOB 1 left it (fm1_filter.h can now sit between two knob steps).
KNOB 4 no longer changes weapon (SELECT and OCT-/OCT+ do); the frame rate moves from ENV to GLO;
EDIT puts all of the sound back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
